571	Form 941-V,
572	Payment Voucher
573	Purpose of Form
574	
575	Specific Instructions
576	
577	Complete Form 941-V if you’re making a payment with
578	Form 941. We will use the completed voucher to credit
579	your payment more promptly and accurately, and to
580	improve our service to you.
581	
582	Box 1—Employer identification number (EIN). If you
583	don’t have an EIN, you may apply for one online by going
584	to www.irs.gov/EIN. You may also apply for an EIN by
585	faxing or mailing Form SS-4 to the IRS. If you haven’t
586	received your EIN by the due date of Form 941, write
587	“Applied For” and the date you applied in this entry space.
588	Box 2—Amount paid. Enter the amount paid with
589	Form 941.
590	Box 3—Tax period. Darken the circle identifying the
591	quarter for which the payment is made. Darken only
592	one circle.
593	Box 4—Name and address. Enter your name and
594	address as shown on Form 941.
595	• Enclose your check or money order made payable to
596	“United States Treasury.” Be sure to enter your
597	EIN, “Form 941,” and the tax period (“1st Quarter 2025,”
598	“2nd Quarter 2025,” “3rd Quarter 2025,” or “4th Quarter
599	2025”) on your check or money order. Don’t send cash.
600	Don’t staple Form 941-V or your payment to Form 941 (or
601	to each other).
602	• Detach Form 941-V and send it with your payment
603	and Form 941 to the address in the Instructions for
604	Form 941.
605	Note: You must also complete the entity information
606	above Part 1 on Form 941.
607	
608	Making Payments With Form 941
609	To avoid a penalty, make your payment with Form 941
610	only if:
611	• Your total taxes after adjustments and nonrefundable
612	credits (Form 941, line 12) for either the current quarter or
613	the preceding quarter are less than $2,500, you didn’t
614	incur a $100,000 next-day deposit obligation during the
615	current quarter, and you’re paying in full with a timely filed
616	return; or
617	• You’re a monthly schedule depositor making a
618	payment in accordance with the accuracy of deposits
619	rule. See section 11 of Pub. 15 for details. In this case,
620	the amount of your payment may be $2,500 or more.
621	Otherwise, you must make deposits by electronic funds
622	transfer. See section 11 of Pub. 15 for deposit
623	instructions. Don’t use Form 941-V to make federal tax
624	deposits.
625	Use Form 941-V when making any payment with
626	! Form 941. However, if you pay an amount with
627	CAUTION
628	Form 941 that should’ve been deposited, you
629	may be subject to a penalty. See Deposit Penalties in
630	section 11 of Pub. 15.
